<title>CANADA: Canada monthly GDP rises 0.1 percent in Sept.</title>
<headline>Canada monthly GDP rises 0.1 percent in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's real gross domestic product, seasonally adjusted, rose 0.1 percent in September after rising 0.1 percent (revised from 0.2 percent) in August, Statistics Canada said on Thursday.</p>
<p>A Reuters survey of economists had forecast real GDP to rise 0.3 percent in September.  </p>
<p>GDP		     Sept 96 chg    Aug 96 chg</p>
<p>Total economy	 552.58  +0.1     +0.1</p>
<p>Goods industries    189.06  -0.1     +0.3</p>
<p>Service industries  363.52  +0.2     +0.1</p>
<p>Business sector     462.83  +0.1     +0.2</p>
<p>Non-business	   89.75  -0.1     +0.1</p>
<p>Note: GDP figures are in billions of dollars, seasonally adjusted at annual rates at factor cost, constant 1986 dollars.</p>
</text>
